WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.122
- Welcome back y'all I'm
here with Adam Lambert,

00:00:02.122 --> 00:00:02.955
give I up!

00:00:02.955 --> 00:00:05.592
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:08.900
Out next guest is a tennis icon.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.830
She has won 73 titles,
four Olympic gold medals

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.300
and seven grand slams in her career

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.640
that has spanned two decades.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.750
Joining us all the way from Australia,

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.240
where she's about to play
in the Australian open.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.731
Please, everybody welcome Venus Williams.

00:00:24.731 --> 00:00:25.890
(upbeat music)

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.549
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:29.549 --> 00:00:33.100
Oh my gosh hello and
say hi to Adam as well.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.550
- Hey Adam, how are you?

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.240
I'm huge fans of both of you.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.970
And I got to listen to the conversation

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.148
you guys had, love the shoes.

00:00:41.148 --> 00:00:43.880
(both laughing)

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.430
I'm glad we are like the Talking Heads,

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:46.973
we should start a group.

00:00:46.973 --> 00:00:48.260
(both laughing)

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.480
- Well, there was the Talking Heads.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.020
So Venus, the Australian
open is your first tournament

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.340
after a pretty big break right?

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.240
- Yeah. My last time it was a French open,

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.520
which happened in October.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.680
Normally it happens in May,

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.500
so all of us are pretty subject
to what's going on in COVID

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.103
but super grateful to be here.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:11.470
Currently just, you
know, enjoying the sun.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.750
It's summertime down here.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.380
So I'm getting all the summertime fruits,

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.740
cherries, all the things
we don't get right now.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.573
- Oh, that's awesome.

00:01:17.573 --> 00:01:20.250
I love Australia, but Venus

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.700
I have to say Serena was just here

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.190
and is also playing in the tournament.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.260
So what's it like
playing with your sister?

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:30.760
- Yeah, we have been
playing doubles together

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.480
honestly since we were eight years old.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.560
So a lot of people know us for maybe

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:36.510
playing against each other

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.120
but we have done so much
together on the court.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.020
It's the best feeling.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.930
I'm still the big sister
and a lot of people ask me

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.940
what are your favorite
moments in the court?

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:47.990
And I'm always like, oh my gosh,
when I play with my sister.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.680
- Yeah. Oh, that's gotta be
such a cool thing too, to have

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.210
especially in this time
where you're not allowed

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.060
you kind of have to create your own pod

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.740
like to still be able to kind of play.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.070
I mean, your sister you all (indistinct)

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:58.500
to be able to even play
against each other.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.383
And I think you're both so gifted.

00:02:00.383 --> 00:02:03.450
Like God, like planted a lifelong partner

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.420
for you to just challenge yourself with

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:08.110
tennis wise, it's amazing, it's so cool.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:11.370
Well, Venus, when you look
back on your tennis career

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.660
what are you most proud of?

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:13.730
'Cause you have an illustrious career

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.600
not just in tennis in a lot of fields

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:19.020
but with tennis specifically,
what are you most proud of?

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.710
- I think I'm most proud of a few things.

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:25.060
And in life you have to enjoy it.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:25.980
If you aren't enjoying it

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.820
no matter what you do, it's not worth it.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:30.440
So I've had a lot of wins.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.580
I've had a lot of losses

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:35.690
but being able to enjoy my time
and look back on fond memory

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:38.500
and all those times the good
ones and the tougher ones.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.310
And of course fighting for equal

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.660
prize money for women on tour,

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.980
because you know, a little known fact

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.420
or maybe well-known fact
that it wasn't always equal

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.720
for women up until 2007,
that wasn't very long ago.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.420
So of course there's a lot of battles

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.560
to fight in this world,

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.390
and I'm looking forward
to continuing to fighting.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.960
Fighting for equality I'm
very passionate about,

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.020
equality for all people of course,

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.980
and of children also.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.390
Super, super passionate about kids

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.500
and giving them an equal
opportunity for good life.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.140
- Absolutely, opportunity is the key.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.390
And I think that's the
most important thing

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:17.340
especially with kids to
set them up for success.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.540
So I found this out, I didn't know this

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.730
but will Smith is
actually playing your dad

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:23.550
in an upcoming movie right?

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.680
- Yeah. So there's this film coming out

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.200
this year now it's called

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.010
or I imagine it will be
this year "King Richard".

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.030
And it's very exciting.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:35.550
It's really about my dad

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:39.730
and how he literally changed
the game and how this started.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:43.370
He's a revolutionary kind of
person and I love him to death.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:46.850
And my mom of course, is
also featured in the movie,

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:49.760
and there's my mom, she's the
coolest lady on the planet.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.060
And she's so fun.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.260
But the two young ladies
that played both Serena and I

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.110
they acted just like Serena and I did,

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.490
holding hands, hugging each other,

00:03:58.490 --> 00:03:59.920
like how we were as kids.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.440
We still like, you know

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.430
hug each other and you
know, it's the same thing.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:06.270
So it was really
interesting to see that kind

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.880
of dynamic on the set.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.660
And we had a lot of fun with them

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.600
because we would say, you
know, just be careful because

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.540
in the year 2000 and we
pretend they were actually us

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.080
you're gonna meet this guy.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:18.776
Don't date him.

00:04:18.776 --> 00:04:20.370
(both laughing)

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.675
- Just say no.

00:04:21.675 --> 00:04:23.940
- We had a lot of fun,
those girls are sharper

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.600
than we ever were at that age though,

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.477
so we don't think we
have to worry about them.

00:04:27.477 --> 00:04:29.000
- Oh my God, that's so funny.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.650
You're gonna meet this guy and just run.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:36.790
Well, Venus did your parents
also inspire the business woman

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.670
in you 'cause you also
have that empire going on?

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.490
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.220
My parents are everything
for me, everything.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.240
And I think that's everyone's parents

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.700
and you learn the good and the bad,

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:49.860
and the ugly from them, right?

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:53.904
And thankfully, my parents
was, you know 95% good.

00:04:53.904 --> 00:04:56.571
(both laughing)

00:05:00.104 --> 00:05:03.230
And they gave us this
entrepreneurial spirit.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:06.030
My dad was born in 1942 in Louisiana.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.530
So pretty hostile conditions
for an African-American man

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:12.270
if you could imagine
growing up in Jim Crow.

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:15.280
So he wanted us to have
these opportunities

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.180
that he didn't have,

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.010
and so he encouraged entrepreneurship.

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:22.753
So I started my own active
wear company called EleVen.

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:26.630
And it's all about the
pursuit of your best self

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.290
and going past that 10 and being 11,

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:33.460
and helping people to be
well and to be their best.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.910
And that is what has
given me my best life,

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.110
is being well and being my best.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:40.530
It builds confidence to
be active and to be well.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.270
- Speaking of that, you have something

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.260
and I just love the name.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:44.470
So I have to bring it up.

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:46.020
It's Happy Viking.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.310
So what is Happy Viking?

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:51.980
- Okay. So last month
we launched Happy Viking

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:55.064
and it's a plant-based protein company

00:05:55.064 --> 00:05:58.910
and the name Happy Viking is about fueling

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:01.680
your inner fighter and your inner vikings.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:04.620
We all know kind of the
reputation of vikings,

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.680
while just feeling happy and satisfied

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.190
with what you put in your body.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:10.040
And it was so exciting

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:13.280
because it's sold out in
less than 24 hours so.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:14.113
- Wow.

00:06:14.113 --> 00:06:15.050
- We're back in stock now

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:20.050
and you can find it at
happyviking.com and elevenbyvenus.com

00:06:20.987 --> 00:06:22.620
and Amazon, of course.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:26.390
And so it's available in
vanilla and chocolate.

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.830
So depending on what
kind of person you are

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:29.777
- I like both.

00:06:29.777 --> 00:06:32.950
- (indistinct) and it's got yellow pea

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.840
and brown rice proteins

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.970
and also macronutrients.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:42.570
And it has Omega three,
sunflower oil, fiber

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:45.576
all nine amino acids,

00:06:45.576 --> 00:06:46.910
and all these different things.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.280
So it's really a different kind of protein

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.890
because it helps your body and your mind

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.382
in the macronutrients.

00:06:53.382 --> 00:06:55.840
So I'm very proud of it.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.580
I'm so excited to help
people to be healthy

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.420
and well on all kinds of platforms.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.450
And that's my mission.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:02.580
- Venus is happy.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.477
Viking products are
available online right now.

